      'To say where it hurts Italian uses **fare male** with a pronoun: **Mi fa male la testa** (“the head hurts me”). The verb agrees with the thing that hurts, so for several things it is **fanno**: **Mi fanno male i piedi.** The doctor asks formally: **Che cosa Le fa male?** You can also use **avere mal di** + body part: **Ho mal di testa**, **mal di gola**, **mal di pancia**. Illnesses use **avere** too: **Ho la febbre**, **Ho la tosse**. Add how long with **da**: **da tre giorni** (“for three days”).',
