      'To talk about what did not happen, build on **avere** or **essere** + the past participle. The **condizionale passato** uses the conditional of the auxiliary: **Avrei dovuto studiare di più** (“I should have studied more”), **Sarei venuto** (“I would have come”). The **congiuntivo trapassato** uses the imperfect subjunctive of the auxiliary: **avessi saputo**, **fossi andato**. Together they make the “if I had…, I would have…” sentence: **Se avessi studiato, avrei superato l’esame.** **Peccato!** expresses regret: **Peccato! Ho perso l’occasione.** **rimpiangere** means “to regret”.',
